    <h1>MuscleTech 100% Mass Gainer Vanilla Milkshake Review (2025)</h1>
        <div id="oos" style="background:#fdf8ec; border:2px solid #e07a2f; border-radius:10px; padding:22px 26px; margin:26px 0;">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 10px; color:#c46a10; font-size:18px;">⚠️ Out of stock on Amazon — here's what to buy instead</h3>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px; line-height:1.65;">
                <strong>MuscleTech 100% Mass Gainer is currently unavailable on Amazon</strong> (both flavors, as of July 2026).
                It keeps its #1 safety ranking because that's what the testing shows &mdash; lead was <strong>not detected</strong>,
                and we don't reorder rankings around stock levels. But you can't buy it right now, so here's where to go.
            </p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 12px; line-height:1.65;">
                <strong>First, check you actually want a mass gainer.</strong> This is a <strong>bulking product</strong> &mdash;
                60g protein and <strong>1,500 calories</strong> per serving. If you're just looking for a safe everyday protein,
                a mass gainer is the wrong tool and you'll gain fat you didn't ask for.
            </p>
            <table style="margin:0;">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>If you want…</th><th>Buy this instead</th><th>Lead result</th><th></th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
